comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-25T07:12:47.062Z","harness:claude-code","Duplicate-check evidence (all-status pm search over unknown subcommand, suggested_retry, did-you-mean, positional, recovery): matched closed pm-8nyc, pm-r2kd, pm-bu1m, pm-zwl7 and open pm-g543, pm-gdi7, pm-ulqu, pm-mpbb. pm-g543 is top-level command ranking, pm-gdi7 is unknown-option suggestion, pm-ulqu is enum value-domain rendering inside an existing suggested_retry, pm-r2kd was a single command silently falling back to list. None covers positional subcommand tokens across families. Filed as a child of pm-mpbb."
  "2026-07-25T07:12:48.039Z","harness:claude-code","Reproduction on 2026.7.25, exact --json .code values: pm schema add-typ Foo -> unknown_subcommand (detail carries the full 15-token allowed set; title truncates it mid-list with an ellipsis). pm graph analyz -> invalid_argument_value (allowed set present in detail). pm plan sttus -> command_failed (allowed set present in detail; the code says execution failure for what is an input error). pm schema add type Foo -> invalid_command_usage with detail 'error: too many arguments for schema. Expected 2 arguments but got 3: add, type, Foo' and no allowed set at all. None of the four returns suggested_retry, although each mistake is edit distance 1 (or a pure hyphenation difference) from a valid token and the allowed set is available at the failure site. The space-form trap is invited by pm schema --help, which renders the subcommand list as 'add/remove type/status/field' rather than the literal tokens add-type, add-status, add-field, remove-type, remove-field."
  "2026-08-10T18:09:14.581Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: introduced the public SDK createUnknownSubcommandError primitive and migrated plan, merge, schema, profile, telemetry, workspace snapshot, graph, config, package/extension lifecycle, and bundled templates refusal families. Contracts expose sorted complete allowed_values, stable unknown_subcommand/reason, safe nearest retries, compatibility aliasing for unknown_lifecycle_action, and public SDK packaging. Verification: exact 100% coverage across 7,187 tests plus packed npm/npx/bun/bunx CLI and SDK-import acceptance in a fresh temporary project."
  "2026-08-10T18:41:17.375Z","harness:codex","Review feedback: DeepScan PR #968 identified the now-unused original subcommand parameter on assertKnownPlanSubcommand after normalization moved into the shared recovery contract. Removing it and its call-site argument; no behavior change."
  "2026-08-10T18:42:02.406Z","harness:codex","Review resolution: removed the unused pre-normalization subcommand parameter and call argument. Focused plan lifecycle, CLI guidance, and SDK recovery tests passed; ESLint and build passed."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-10T18:09:26.804Z","harness:codex",A universal refusal primitive should carry the complete sorted vocabulary and add a retry only when similarity or the caller provides a safe replacement; installed-package acceptance guards the public bundle barrel.
